# The Rust code in generated/rust/ is generated from the Python code in system/ and never edited by hand (see
# generated/rust/README.md): GitLab folds its files in merge request diffs, GitHub marks them as generated. The files
# that control the build and its dependencies stay unfolded, so reviewers see changes to them. Line endings stay LF,
# as in the Rust code the generator writes.
generated/rust/** gitlab-generated linguist-generated text eol=lf
generated/rust/Cargo.toml -gitlab-generated -linguist-generated
generated/rust/Cargo.lock -gitlab-generated -linguist-generated
generated/rust/rust-toolchain.toml -gitlab-generated -linguist-generated
# A test compares the benchmark report byte for byte with a fresh rendering, which has LF line endings:
benchmarks/index.html text eol=lf
# The copies of the Python sources the Rust code was generated from (see generated/python_sources/README.md): written
# by .ci/check_generated.py --update, folded in merge request diffs; their README stays unfolded. Git never converts
# the line endings of a copy, as its name is the hash of its exact bytes; the README is ordinary text.
generated/python_sources/** gitlab-generated linguist-generated -text
generated/python_sources/README.md -gitlab-generated -linguist-generated text=auto
